libmimalloc-sys 0.1.44 (feature `v3` = bundled mimalloc 3.1.5): fix the two-level page map on 32-bit targets.
- On a 32-bit target the two-level page map (what mimalloc selects on Apple) has 16 top-level entries and
  32-bit commit words, so MI_PAGE_MAP_ENTRIES_PER_CBIT = 16/32 = 0 and `idx / 0` in mi_page_map_is_committed
  is a division by a constant zero. GCC -O2 turns that into __builtin_trap(), so mi_page_map_ensure_committed
  is an unconditional `trap` and the very first allocation (page map init) dies with SIGTRAP (skim 5.7.3 `sk`).
- This is upstream mimalloc 3fed338716 "fix 2 level page map for 32 bit" (first in 3.3.0, so libmimalloc-sys
  0.1.45+ already has it). 0.1.43 and earlier have no v3 tree; the v2 copy (2.2.4) has no page map.

--- a/c_src/mimalloc/v3/src/page-map.c
+++ b/c_src/mimalloc/v3/src/page-map.c
@@ -189,7 +189,7 @@
 // divide the main map in 64 (`MI_BFIELD_BITS`) parts commit those parts on demand
 static _Atomic(mi_bfield_t)  mi_page_map_commit;
 
-#define MI_PAGE_MAP_ENTRIES_PER_CBIT  (MI_PAGE_MAP_COUNT / MI_BFIELD_BITS)
+#define MI_PAGE_MAP_ENTRIES_PER_CBIT  (MI_PAGE_MAP_COUNT < MI_BFIELD_BITS ? 1 : (MI_PAGE_MAP_COUNT / MI_BFIELD_BITS))
 
 static inline bool mi_page_map_is_committed(size_t idx, size_t* pbit_idx) {
   mi_bfield_t commit = mi_atomic_load_relaxed(&mi_page_map_commit);
